---
// The men's group in Charlotte, VT: what it is, the places filled so far, who it's for, its four
// rounds on a wheel, and the application form (with an optional video), which posts to /api/apply.
// The wheel: Lover starts at the top; clicking turns it a quarter counter-clockwise to the next
// round (or straight to the round clicked) and the explanation beside it follows. Without
// JavaScript every explanation shows, the video part is hidden, and the form posts itself; the
// page's #applied and #apply-failed notes answer it.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { GROUP } from '../data/mens-group';

type Round = { id: string; name: string; weeks: string; element: string; line: string; color: string; ink: string; body: string[]; shadow: string };

// Colours follow each archetype's element in Cliff Barry's Shadow Work map of the four (water,
// earth, air, fire): Kazan for the Lover's water, burnt sienna for the Warrior's earth, Hackberry
// for the Magician, Beach gold for the King's fire. Clockwise from the top the wheel keeps that
// map's order (King north, Lover east, Warrior south, Magician west), turned so Lover leads.
const rounds: Round[] = [
  {
    id: 'lover',
    name: 'Lover',
    weeks: 'Weeks 1–3',
    element: 'Water',
    line: 'Feeling, connection and aliveness.',
    color: 'var(--kazan)',
    ink: '#fff',
    body: [
      'The Lover is the part of a man that feels: joy, grief, desire, beauty, the plain pleasure of being alive. We begin here because a circle is built on connection.',
      'These weeks are for getting to know each other, slowing down, and learning to say what is actually going on inside.',
    ],
    shadow: 'Chasing more and more sensation, or going numb and feeling nothing at all.',
  },
  {
    id: 'warrior',
    name: 'Warrior',
    weeks: 'Weeks 4–6',
    element: 'Earth',
    line: 'Purpose, boundaries and commitment.',
    color: '#a3472a',
    ink: '#fff',
    body: [
      'The Warrior is energy in service of something: a clear aim, discipline, the courage to act and the courage to say no.',
      'These weeks look at what you are fighting for, where your yes and your no are clear and where they aren’t, and the commitments you keep and the ones you avoid.',
    ],
    shadow: 'Turning harsh and controlling, or collapsing and never showing up for the fight.',
  },
  {
    id: 'magician',
    name: 'Magician',
    weeks: 'Weeks 7–9',
    element: 'Air',
    line: 'Awareness, insight and change.',
    color: 'var(--hackberry)',
    ink: '#fff',
    body: [
      'The Magician sees beneath the surface: the patterns we repeat, the stories we tell ourselves, the feelings behind our reactions.',
      'These weeks turn the circle’s attention inward, to the beliefs and old wounds that run us, and to how they change once they are seen.',
    ],
    shadow: 'Using what he knows to manipulate, or playing innocent to avoid responsibility.',
  },
  {
    id: 'king',
    name: 'King',
    weeks: 'Weeks 10–12',
    element: 'Fire',
    line: 'Order, blessing and leadership.',
    color: 'var(--beach)',
    ink: 'var(--fg)',
    body: [
      'The King holds the whole: he sets a direction, makes order, and blesses the people around him.',
      'The last round brings the first three together, feeling, purpose and insight, into a mature way of leading your own life, your family and your work. We close the circle in the final week.',
    ],
    shadow: 'Becoming a tyrant, or a weakling who gives his power away.',
  },
];

const needed = GROUP.size - GROUP.filled;
const words = ['no', 'one', 'two', 'three', 'four', 'five'];
const description = `A men’s group in Charlotte, Vermont, weekly for three months in four rounds: Lover, Warrior, Magician and King. ${GROUP.filled} of ${GROUP.size} places filled; it begins once five men are accepted.`;
---

<Base title="Join a Men’s Group, Charlotte VT · Samperet.com" description={description} path="/mens-group/">
  <main class="wrap mg">
    <a class="arrow-link home-btn" href="/" data-track="nav:home"><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">←</span> Home</a>

    <header class="mg-head">
      <h1>Join a men’s group, Charlotte VT</h1>
      <p class="lede">Weekly for three months, in four rounds: Lover, Warrior, Magician and King.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="seats">
      <ol class="seat-row" aria-hidden="true">
        {Array.from({ length: GROUP.size }, (_, i) => <li class:list={['seat', { filled: i < GROUP.filled }]} />)}
      </ol>
      <p>
        <strong>{GROUP.filled} of {GROUP.size} places filled.</strong>{' '}
        {needed > 0 ? `${words[needed][0].toUpperCase()}${words[needed].slice(1)} more ${needed === 1 ? 'man' : 'men'} needed to begin.` : 'The circle is full.'}
      </p>
    </div>

    <dl class="mg-facts">
      <div><dt>Cost</dt><dd>Your commitment and accountability</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Meets</dt><dd>Weekly, for three months</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Rounds</dt><dd>Four, three weeks each</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Time, place &amp; start date</dt><dd>Set once five men are accepted</dd></div>
    </dl>

    <div class="mg-intro measure">
      <p>
        A small circle of men, meeting once a week to be honest about our lives: what we feel, what we want, where we are stuck, and what we are
        here to do. No one is fixed or lectured; each man is met, heard and challenged by the others.
      </p>
      <p>
        I have joined and built men’s circles since my initiation into the ManKind Project in 2012, and have led circles of healing and
        transformation since 2016. The rounds follow the four archetypes of mature masculinity that Robert Moore and Douglas Gillette
        describe in <cite>King, Warrior, Magician, Lover</cite>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="mg-who" aria-labelledby="who-title">
      <h2 id="who-title">Who I’m looking for</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Men who want to take responsibility for their lives, and support the men around them to do the same.</li>
        <li>Men who can fix shit, from cars to relationships.</li>
        <li>Men who can say the hard thing, who don’t ask for permission when none is needed, and who pave the way for the man behind them.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mg-rounds" aria-labelledby="rounds-title">
      <h2 id="rounds-title">The four rounds</h2>
      <p class="muted mg-hint">Click the wheel to turn it to the next round.</p>

      <div class="rounds-layout">
        <div class="wheel" data-wheel style="--turn: 0deg">
          <span class="wheel-pointer" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="wheel-disc">
            {
              rounds.map((r, i) => (
                <button
                  type="button"
                  class="wedge"
                  data-wedge={i}
                  aria-label={`${r.name}, round ${i + 1}`}
                  aria-controls={`round-${r.id}-panel`}
                  aria-pressed={i === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'}
                  style={`--at: ${i * 90}deg; --c: ${r.color}; --ink: ${r.ink}`}
                  data-track={`mens-group:wheel:${r.id}`}
                >
                  <span class="wedge-label">
                    <span class="wedge-name">{r.name}</span>
                    <span class="wedge-weeks">{r.weeks}</span>
                  </span>
                </button>
              ))
            }
          </div>
          <button type="button" class="wheel-hub" data-next data-track="mens-group:wheel:next">
            <span class="hub-count">Round <span data-hub>1</span> of 4</span>
            <span class="hub-next">Next <span aria-hidden="true">↺</span></span>
          </button>
        </div>

        <div class="round-panels" aria-live="polite">
          {
            rounds.map((r, i) => (
              <div class="round-panel" id={`round-${r.id}-panel`} style={`--c: ${r.color}`} hidden={i !== 0}>
                <p class="round-panel-meta">
                  Round {i + 1} · {r.weeks} · {r.element}
                </p>
                <h3>{r.name}</h3>
                <p class="round-line">{r.line}</p>
                {r.body.map((p) => <p>{p}</p>)}
                <p class="round-shadow">
                  <strong>In shadow:</strong> {r.shadow}
                </p>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
      <noscript><style>.round-panel[hidden] { display: block; } .round-panel + .round-panel { margin-top: var(--s6); }</style></noscript>
    </section>

    <section class="mg-apply" id="apply" aria-labelledby="apply-title">
      <h2 id="apply-title">Apply to join</h2>
      <p class="muted measure">
        The group begins once five men have been accepted; {words[needed]} more {needed === 1 ? 'place is' : 'places are'} open. I’ll read every
        application and write back to each of you, and to those accepted with the time, place and start date.
      </p>

      <p class="mg-note mg-done" id="applied" tabindex="-1" data-done>
        <strong>Thank you<span data-done-name></span>.</strong> Your application is in. Once five men have been accepted, I’ll write to you
        with the time, place and start date.
      </p>
      <p class="mg-note mg-failed" id="apply-failed" tabindex="-1">
        That didn’t go through. Try again, or write to <a href="mailto:sam@peret.net?subject=Men%E2%80%99s%20group">sam@peret.net</a>.
      </p>

      <form class="mg-form" method="post" action="/api/apply" enctype="multipart/form-data" data-apply>
        <div class="field-row">
          <label class="field">
            <span>Name</span>
            <input name="name" autocomplete="name" maxlength="100" required />
          </label>
          <label class="field">
            <span>Email</span>
            <input name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" maxlength="200" required />
          </label>
        </div>
        <div class="field-row">
          <label class="field">
            <span>Phone <em>optional</em></span>
            <input name="phone" type="tel" autocomplete="tel" maxlength="50" />
          </label>
          <label class="field">
            <span>Where do you live? <em>optional</em></span>
            <input name="lives" autocomplete="address-level2" maxlength="200" placeholder="Town" />
          </label>
        </div>
        <label class="field">
          <span>What draws you to the group?</span>
          <textarea name="why" rows="5" maxlength="4000" required></textarea>
        </label>

        <fieldset class="video" data-video hidden>
          <legend>A short video: when have you felt most alive? <em>optional, up to a minute</em></legend>
          <p class="muted">
            Record your answer here with your camera and microphone. It comes to me with your application, as an email attachment, and is not
            published or kept on this site.
          </p>
          <div class="video-stage" data-stage>
            <video class="video-live" data-live playsinline muted hidden></video>
            <video class="video-take" data-take playsinline controls hidden></video>
            <p class="video-question" data-question>When have you felt most alive?</p>
            <span class="video-count" data-count aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="video-clock" data-clock hidden>0:00 / 1:00</span>
          </div>
          <div class="video-controls">
            <button type="button" class="btn" data-camera>Turn on camera</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-accent" data-record hidden><span class="rec-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> Record</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" data-stop hidden>Stop</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-quiet" data-again hidden>Record again</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-quiet" data-remove hidden>Remove video</button>
          </div>
          <p class="video-status" data-status aria-live="polite"></p>
        </fieldset>

        <label class="field">
          <span>Have you sat in a men’s circle, or done other men’s work, before? <em>optional</em></span>
          <textarea name="experience" rows="3" maxlength="4000"></textarea>
        </label>
        <label class="field">
          <span>Which days and times usually work for you? <em>optional</em></span>
          <input name="times" maxlength="1000" placeholder="Weekday evenings, Sunday mornings…" />
        </label>
        <label class="check">
          <input type="checkbox" name="commit" value="yes" required />
          <span>I can commit to meeting weekly for three months, and to being accountable to the group.</span>
        </label>
        <div class="hp" aria-hidden="true">
          <label>Website <input name="website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" /></label>
        </div>
        <p class="mg-error" role="alert" data-error></p>
        <div class="mg-submit">
          <button type="submit" class="btn btn-accent" data-track="mens-group:apply">Send my application <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button>
          <span class="muted" data-sending></span>
        </div>
      </form>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script>
    import fixWebmDuration from 'fix-webm-duration';
    import { sessionId, startTracking, track } from '../scripts/track';

    startTracking();

    // ---- The wheel ----
    // Each wedge sits at a quarter turn (Lover 0°, Warrior 90°, Magician 180°, King 270°). The disc
    // only ever turns counter-clockwise, a quarter per round, so `turn` keeps growing more negative
    // and the round at the top is the one whose angle cancels it.
    const wheel = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-wheel]')!;
    const wedges = [...wheel.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-wedge]')];
    const hub = wheel.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-hub]')!;
    let step = 0; // quarter turns so far
    const current = () => step % wedges.length;

    const turnTo = (index: number, animate = true) => {
      const ahead = (index - current() + wedges.length) % wedges.length;
      step += ahead;
      wheel.classList.toggle('still', !animate);
      wheel.style.setProperty('--turn', `${step * -90}deg`);
      for (const [i, wedge] of wedges.entries()) {
        const on = i === index;
        wedge.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(on));
        document.getElementById(wedge.getAttribute('aria-controls')!)!.hidden = !on;
      }
      hub.textContent = String(index + 1);
    };
    const next = () => turnTo((current() + 1) % wedges.length);

    // Clicking the round at the top, or the hub, moves on; clicking another round turns it to the top.
    for (const [i, wedge] of wedges.entries()) {
      wedge.addEventListener('click', () => (i === current() ? next() : turnTo(i)));
    }
    wheel.querySelector('[data-next]')!.addEventListener('click', next);

    // A link to a round (#warrior) opens on it.
    const fromHash = () => {
      const i = wedges.findIndex((w) => w.getAttribute('aria-controls') === `round-${location.hash.slice(1)}-panel`);
      if (i >= 0) turnTo(i, false);
    };
    addEventListener('hashchange', fromHash);
    fromHash();

    // ---- The video: when have you felt most alive? ----
    const LIMIT = 60; // seconds
    const MAX_BYTES = 4_200_000; // under Vercel's 4.5 MB request limit, with the rest of the form
    const videoBox = document.querySelector<HTMLFieldSetElement>('[data-video]')!;
    const live = videoBox.querySelector<HTMLVideoElement>('[data-live]')!;
    const takeView = videoBox.querySelector<HTMLVideoElement>('[data-take]')!;
    const question = videoBox.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-question]')!;
    const countEl = videoBox.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-count]')!;
    const clockEl = videoBox.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-clock]')!;
    const status = videoBox.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-status]')!;
    const buttons = {
      camera: videoBox.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-camera]')!,
      record: videoBox.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-record]')!,
      stop: videoBox.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-stop]')!,
      again: videoBox.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-again]')!,
      remove: videoBox.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-remove]')!,
    };
    type ButtonName = keyof typeof buttons;
    const showButtons = (...names: ButtonName[]) => {
      for (const [name, button] of Object.entries(buttons)) button.hidden = !names.includes(name as ButtonName);
    };

    const clock = (s: number) => `${Math.floor(s / 60)}:${String(Math.floor(s % 60)).padStart(2, '0')}`;
    const sleep = (ms: number) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));
    const pickType = (types: string[]) => types.find((t) => MediaRecorder.isTypeSupported(t)) ?? '';

    let stream: MediaStream | undefined;
    let recorder: MediaRecorder | undefined;
    let take: { blob: Blob; seconds: number } | undefined;
    let takeUrl = '';

    const canRecord = typeof MediaRecorder !== 'undefined' && !!navigator.mediaDevices?.getUserMedia;
    if (canRecord) videoBox.hidden = false;

    const stopCamera = () => {
      stream?.getTracks().forEach((t) => t.stop());
      stream = undefined;
      live.srcObject = null;
      live.hidden = true;
    };

    const clearTake = () => {
      take = undefined;
      if (takeUrl) URL.revokeObjectURL(takeUrl);
      takeUrl = '';
      takeView.removeAttribute('src');
      takeView.hidden = true;
    };

    const cameraOn = async () => {
      status.textContent = '';
      buttons.camera.disabled = true;
      try {
        stream = await navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia({
          video: { facingMode: 'user', width: { ideal: 640 }, height: { ideal: 480 } },
          audio: { echoCancellation: true, noiseSuppression: true },
        });
      } catch {
        status.textContent = 'The camera didn’t turn on. Allow this page to use your camera and microphone, or apply without a video.';
        buttons.camera.disabled = false;
        return;
      }
      buttons.camera.disabled = false;
      clearTake();
      live.srcObject = stream;
      live.hidden = false;
      void live.play().catch(() => {});
      question.classList.add('over');
      showButtons('record');
      status.textContent = 'When you’re ready, press Record. You have up to a minute.';
    };

    const record = async () => {
      if (!stream) return;
      showButtons();
      for (const n of [3, 2, 1]) {
        countEl.textContent = String(n);
        await sleep(800);
      }
      countEl.textContent = '';

      const type = pickType([
        'video/mp4;codecs=avc1.42E01E,mp4a.40.2',
        'video/mp4;codecs=avc1,mp4a',
        'video/webm;codecs=vp8,opus',
        'video/webm;codecs=vp9,opus',
        'video/webm',
        'video/mp4',
      ]);
      const chunks: Blob[] = [];
      recorder = new MediaRecorder(stream, { ...(type && { mimeType: type }), videoBitsPerSecond: 350_000, audioBitsPerSecond: 48_000 });
      recorder.ondataavailable = (e) => e.data.size && chunks.push(e.data);
      const started = performance.now();
      const stopped = new Promise((r) => recorder!.addEventListener('stop', r, { once: true }));
      recorder.start(1000);
      showButtons('stop');
      clockEl.hidden = false;
      status.textContent = 'Recording…';
      const tick = setInterval(() => {
        const s = (performance.now() - started) / 1000;
        clockEl.textContent = `${clock(s)} / ${clock(LIMIT)}`;
        if (s >= LIMIT && recorder?.state === 'recording') recorder.stop();
      }, 250);

      await stopped;
      clearInterval(tick);
      const seconds = (performance.now() - started) / 1000;
      clockEl.hidden = true;
      stopCamera();
      question.classList.remove('over');

      let blob = new Blob(chunks, { type: recorder.mimeType || type || 'video/webm' });
      // Chrome's WebM carries no duration, so players can't show its length or seek; write it in.
      if (blob.type.includes('webm')) blob = await fixWebmDuration(blob, seconds * 1000, { logger: false });
      if (blob.size > MAX_BYTES) {
        status.textContent = 'That take is too large to send. Record a shorter one.';
        showButtons('again');
        return;
      }
      take = { blob, seconds };
      takeUrl = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
      takeView.src = takeUrl;
      takeView.hidden = false;
      showButtons('again', 'remove');
      status.textContent = `Your video (${clock(seconds)}) will be sent with your application.`;
    };

    buttons.camera.addEventListener('click', cameraOn);
    buttons.record.addEventListener('click', () => void record());
    buttons.stop.addEventListener('click', () => recorder?.state === 'recording' && recorder.stop());
    buttons.again.addEventListener('click', cameraOn);
    buttons.remove.addEventListener('click', () => {
      clearTake();
      showButtons('camera');
      status.textContent = 'Video removed.';
    });

    // ---- The form: checked here, sent with the video, answered in place ----
    const form = document.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>('[data-apply]')!;
    const error = form.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-error]')!;
    const sending = form.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-sending]')!;
    const done = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-done]')!;
    const submit = form.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('button[type="submit"]')!;
    form.noValidate = true; // checked below, with messages in the site's voice
    form.addEventListener('input', () => (error.textContent = ''));

    const problem = () => {
      for (const field of form.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement | HTMLTextAreaElement>('input, textarea')) {
        if (field.name === 'website' || field.checkValidity()) continue;
        field.focus();
        if (field.name === 'commit') return 'The group asks for twelve weeks. Tick the box if you can commit to them.';
        if (field.name === 'email' && field.value.trim()) return 'That email address doesn’t look right.';
        const label = field.closest('label')?.querySelector('span')?.textContent?.replace(/optional$/, '').trim();
        return `${label ?? 'This'} is needed.`;
      }
      return null;
    };

    form.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      error.textContent = '';
      const missing = problem();
      if (missing) {
        error.textContent = missing;
        return;
      }
      if (recorder?.state === 'recording') {
        error.textContent = 'Stop the recording first.';
        return;
      }
      const data = new FormData(form);
      data.set('session', sessionId() ?? '');
      if (take) {
        data.set('video', take.blob, `most-alive.${take.blob.type.includes('mp4') ? 'mp4' : 'webm'}`);
        data.set('video_length', clock(take.seconds));
      }
      submit.disabled = true;
      sending.textContent = take ? 'Sending your application and video…' : 'Sending…';
      try {
        const res = await fetch(form.action, { method: 'POST', headers: { Accept: 'application/json' }, body: data });
        const reply = await res.json().catch(() => ({ ok: false }));
        if (!reply.ok) throw new Error(reply.error ?? (res.status === 413 ? 'That video is too large to send. Record a shorter one.' : ''));
        track('click', 'mens-group:applied');
        stopCamera();
        done.querySelector('[data-done-name]')!.textContent = `, ${String(data.get('name')).trim().split(/\s+/)[0]}`;
        done.classList.add('shown');
        form.hidden = true;
        done.focus();
      } catch (err) {
        error.textContent = err instanceof Error && err.message && err.message !== 'Failed to fetch' ? err.message : 'That didn’t go through. Try again, or write to sam@peret.net.';
      } finally {
        submit.disabled = false;
        sending.textContent = '';
      }
    });
  </script>
</Base>

<style is:global>
  .mg {
    padding: var(--s6) 0 var(--s9);
    display: grid;
  }

  .mg-head {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s3);
    margin: var(--s7) 0 var(--s5);
  }

  .mg-head h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 1.4rem + 5vw, 5rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 1.02;
    max-width: 14ch;
  }

  .mg-head .lede {
    font-size: clamp(1.125rem, 1rem + 1vw, 1.5rem);
  }

  /* ---- Places filled: five seats, the filled ones in the accent ---- */
  .seats {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--s3) var(--s4);
    margin-bottom: var(--s6);
  }

  .seat-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--s2);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .seat {
    width: 1.75rem;
    height: 1.75rem;
    border: 2px dashed var(--rule-strong);
    border-radius: 50%;
  }

  .seat.filled {
    border: 0;
    background: var(--accent);
  }

  .seats p {
    font-size: var(--text-md);
  }

  .seats strong {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* ---- The facts: a row of hairline-topped cells, no boxes ---- */
  .mg-facts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 12rem), 1fr));
    gap: var(--s4) var(--s5);
    margin: 0 0 var(--s7);
  }

  .mg-facts > div {
    padding-top: var(--s3);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--fg);
  }

  .mg-facts dt {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .mg-facts dd {
